# OWW × Document Studio (durable design memory)

When designing or extending **Communications**, **Marketing & SEO**, **Social**, or **CMS/blog** editors in OWW, treat **Document Studio** as the product pattern — do not invent a thinner one-off editor.

## Source of truth

- Agent / rule: `saas-document-studio` (WW360 donor: `StudioEditor`, `studioTemplates.ts`, `studioTemplateFill.ts`)
- OWW catalog: `frontend/src/config/owwStudioTemplates.ts` (audiences + categories + purpose layouts)
- Placeholder helper: `frontend/src/lib/studioTemplateFill.ts`
- TipTap surface: `/admin/studio` Document Studio (`StudioEditor` + folders + versions + screen grab)
- Deep links: `/admin/studio?content_page=`, `?intent=social`, `?template=`

## Required on every design/change

1. **Purpose templates** — new post/email/social types go in `owwStudioTemplates` (category + audience + preview + body/sections). Prefer porting WW360 `studioTemplates` outreach/brief content over rewriting from scratch.
2. **TipTap** — body editing uses RichTextEditor (image/video upload, links, headings). Do not regress to bare `<textarea>` for HTML bodies.
3. **Media** — uploads go through existing CMS media / asset APIs (UUID/unguessable URLs). Hero + media_gallery remain valid section types; inline media uses TipTap.
4. **`{{placeholders}}`** — templates keep tokens (`{{contact_name}}`, `{{state_code}}`, …); fill via `applyStudioPlaceholders` when context is known; leave unknown tokens visible.
5. **Type scale** — body `text-lg` / controls ≥ `text-base` / captions ≥ `text-sm` / touch ≥44px (WW360 accessible type).
6. **Hero outline buttons** — on `OwwPageHero` (navy), never use bare `variant="outline"` alone: inherit of `text-white` + white `bg-background` makes labels invisible. Use `OWW_HERO_OUTLINE_BTN` or rely on the hero actions glass override.

## Do not

- Fork a second rich-text stack or paste raw HTML textareas for new compose UIs.
- Hard-code one-off blog section stacks outside the Studio catalog.
- Invent UEI/secrets into placeholder autofill.
- Drop Document Studio ownership/versioning requirements into OWW CMS unless product asks for a full Studio module — reuse **editor + templates + media + fill** first.
